 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "raid",
   "title": "The raiders push toward the Loire",
   "time": "Summer-autumn 732",
   "narrative": "After beating Duke Odo on the Garonne, the Umayyad army of al-Andalus moved north through Aquitaine. Its fast cavalry had outrun the supply wagons and much of the host, and it split into raiding parties while the main body followed more slowly. The prize may have been the rich abbey of Saint Martin at Tours, the holiest shrine of the West. Abd al-Rahman waited for the harvest before moving, so that the army could eat off the land.",
   "positions": {
