  {
   "id": "frankish-march",
   "title": "Charles marches by stealth",
   "time": "Autumn 732",
   "narrative": "Odo, beaten and short of men, appealed to the Franks, and Charles Martel agreed only after Odo accepted Frankish overlordship. Charles gathered Austrasian Franks and auxiliaries from beyond the Rhine, including Thuringians, Alemanni and Bavarians, and marched south while avoiding the old Roman roads. His aim was to arrive unseen, so that he and not the enemy would choose the ground.",
