   "id": "surprise",
   "title": "The Umayyads find a wall in front of them",
   "time": "Early October 732",
   "narrative": "The invaders were caught off guard to find a large army sitting squarely across their road to Tours. Charles chose not to attack. He drew his men up on high ground with trees before them, in a deep, close formation that Arab sources describe as a great square, so that any cavalry charge would have to climb and thread through timber. The forest also hid how many Franks there really were.",
