   "id": "waiting",
   "title": "A week of skirmishing",
   "time": "c. 3-9 October 732",
   "narrative": "For about a week neither side wished to attack. The Umayyads waited for the rest of their strength to come up and hoped to draw the Franks down into open ground; they could not judge Frankish numbers. Charles, whose men were dressed for the northern cold and whose levies were foraging and harassing the enemy, was content to wait while winter drew nearer and the invaders' food ran short.",
