   "title": "Abd al-Rahman orders the charge",
   "time": "Seventh day, 10 October 732",
   "narrative": "Abd al-Rahman would not wait longer, with winter coming and Tours still unreached. On the seventh day he put his faith in his cavalry and sent it against the hill. The horsemen had to ride uphill and through the trees, which blunted the shock they were used to delivering. The Frankish infantry held its ground in a tight mass.",
