   "id": "repeated-charges",
   "title": "Charge after charge",
   "time": "Through the day",
   "narrative": "The charges came again and again all day. Arab accounts say the horsemen broke into the Frankish square more than once, and western accounts agree the fight was hard. Yet the formation re-closed each time. Charles's veterans, many of them campaigning with him for years, did what contemporaries thought impossible: they stood against heavy cavalry on foot and did not break.",
